Firmware images
---------------

Read-only images of the instruments' own program ROMs, from which the
SCPI command tree in `docs/z3801-tree.md` was extracted and against
which claims about the command set are checked.  CPU32 code, big-endian, loaded at address zero; see
`docs/firmware.md` for which part.

  z3801a-3543.bin            Z3801A firmware, revision 3543.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 1993.
  z3816a-4001.bin            Z3816A firmware, revision 4001.  Copyright
                             Hewlett-Packard 2000.

The revision is the string the firmware puts in the third field of its
`*IDN?` answer, stored just before the image's second copyright notice
(`0x12eee` in the Z3801A image, `0x22ff8` in the Z3816A's).  The letter
that follows it in a real answer, as in 3704-C, is read from RAM and is
not in the image.

Motorola / Synergy Systems
--------------------------

The GPS receiver inside these instruments is a Motorola Oncore, and
the interval the instrument measures has that receiver's 1 PPS at one
end of it, so its message set is as much a part of the specification
as the SCPI manuals.

  VPCommands.pdf             "VP Oncore Command Reference", Synergy
                             Systems, LLC, October 2001.  Compiled and
                             audited against Motorola's Technical
                             Reference Manual TRM0001 version 7.0 of
                             May 1996, and covering the 6 channel
                             PVT-6 and Basic Oncore and the 6 and 8
                             channel VP Oncore.  The Time RAIM setup
                             and status messages it documents, @@Bn
                             for six channels and @@En for eight, are
                             what carry the negative sawtooth residual.
  vponcoreengnotesarchive.pdf
                             "VP Oncore Engineering Notes", Motorola
                             Position and Navigation Systems Business,
                             revision 1.0, August 1996, as archived by
                             Synergy Systems, LLC in July 2002.
                             Specifications, power, antenna, RTC, 1 PPS
                             signal definition and serial interface for
                             the VP Oncore.
  ut-engg-notes.pdf          "Oncore Engineering Note: UT Plus
                             Oncore", Motorola, revision 1.0, March
                             2000.  Mechanical, electrical and 1 PPS
                             detail for the UT+.
  SSR-VP-UT-and-GT-Drop-In-ReplacementsTN484-D-031925.pdf
                             Synergy Systems, LLC tech note #484-D,
                             revised January 2025.  Present-day u-blox
                             based drop-in replacements for the VP, UT+
                             and GT+ Oncore, which do not suffer the
                             1024 week rollover these instruments do.

NIST
----

The reference for the stability estimators, and the source of the
published values the Allan deviation is checked against.

  NIST-SP-1065.pdf           W. J. Riley, "Handbook of Frequency
                             Stability Analysis", NIST Special
                             Publication 1065, July 2008.  Section 12.4
                             defines a 1000-point test data set and
                             Table 31 gives its deviations.
